JWasm: -Zj makes TYPE of a symbol not yet defined the constant 0

In pass one MASM 5 gives TYPE of a forward-referenced symbol the value 0,
a constant, not a forward reference: ADD DI,TYPE FTBLK, before FTBLK's
STRUC, is 83 C7 26 in pass two, the sign-extended byte form, with no
padding.  JWasm took the undefined symbol for a near label (FF02h), so
sized it as a word immediate, and flagged the operand as a forward
reference, which 0018 then keeps a word.  Under -Zj, TYPE of an undefined
symbol is 0, and its operand is not a forward reference.

Needed for DISPLAY.SYS' CPS-FUNC.INC, which comes before F-PARSER.INC's
FTBLK STRUC.

diff --git a/src/expreval.c b/src/expreval.c
index b94b0f1..1ec2b22 100644
--- a/src/expreval.c
+++ b/src/expreval.c
